<body>
  <div class="page-wrapper">
    {% include "header-en.njk" %}
    <main class="main-wrapper">
      <div id="section_hero" class="article-hero">
        <div class="padding-global">
          <div class="container-large">
            <div class="heading-style-h1 text-color-alternate text-align-center">Privacy Policy<br></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="section_home_intro" class="section-article">
        <div class="padding-global">
          <div class="container-large">
            <div class="spacer-large"></div>
            <div class="spacer-large"></div>
            <div class="heading-style-h2"><strong>Website</strong></div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="text-size-medium">Our website address is <a href="https://imin2uk.com/"
                class="link_branded">https://imin2uk.com</a>.</div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="heading-style-h2"><strong>Comments</strong></div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="text-size-medium">When visitors leave comments on our site, we may collect the data shown in the
              comments form, as well as the visitor’s IP address, browser type, and other related information. This is
              primarily for spam detection and prevention.</div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="text-size-medium">An anonymised string (also known as a hash) created from the visitor’s email
              address may be provided to the Gravatar service. The Gravatar service privacy policy is available at: <a
                href="https://automattic.com/privacy/" target="_blank"
                class="link_branded">https://automattic.com/privacy/</a>
            </div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="text-size-medium">If a visitor’s comment is approved, their profile picture may be publicly
              visible alongside the comment.</div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="heading-style-h2"><strong>Media</strong></div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="text-size-medium">If visitors upload images or videos to our website, any embedded location data
              (EXIF GPS) included in the files will also be uploaded. Other visitors or site administrators may be able
              to download and extract location data from these files.</div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="heading-style-h2"><strong>Cookies</strong></div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="text-size-medium">If you leave a comment on our site, you may opt to save your name, email
              address, and website in cookies. These will be stored for one year.</div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="text-size-medium">When you visit our login page, we will set a temporary cookie to determine if
              your browser accepts cookies. This cookie contains no personal data and is discarded when you close your
              browser.</div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="text-size-medium">When you log in, we will also set up cookies to save your login details and
              your screen display preferences. Login cookies last for two days, and screen options cookies last for one
              year. If you select “Remember Me”, your login will persist for two weeks. When you log out, login cookies
              will be removed.</div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="text-size-medium">If you edit or publish a post, an additional cookie will be saved in your
              browser. This cookie contains no personal data and simply indicates the post ID of the content you have
              just edited.</div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="heading-style-h2"><strong>Embedded Content from Other Websites</strong></div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="text-size-medium">Articles on our site may include embedded content, such as videos, images, or
              articles. Embedded content from other websites behaves in exactly the same way as if the visitor had
              visited the other website directly.</div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="text-size-medium">If you are logged into an account on our site and interact with embedded
              content from another website, that website may collect data about you and enable tracking or monitoring of
              your interaction.</div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="heading-style-h2"><strong>Data Retention and Your Rights</strong></div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="text-size-medium">If you leave a comment, the comment and its metadata are retained
              indefinitely.</div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="text-size-medium">For users who register on our site, we store the personal information they
              provide in their profile. All users can view, edit, or delete their personal information at any time.
              Website administrators can also view and edit this information.</div>
            <div class="spacer-small"></div>
            <div class="text-size-medium">If you have an account on our site, or have left comments containing personal
              information, you may request to receive an exported file of the personal data we hold about you, or
              request that we erase it. However, we may be obliged to retain certain information for legal or regulatory
              purposes.<br></div>
            <div class="spacer-large"></div>
            <div class="spacer-large"></div>
            <div class="spacer-large"></div>
            <div class="spacer-large"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
